            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis 0.12.0</h2>
<p><b>Tell Jarvis.</b> One place to hand Jarvis what it cannot see — a call on
a platform it does not sync, a decision made in a corridor, or a standing
instruction about what matters to you. It sorts what you write into tasks and
into rules it follows from then on.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Press ⌘J, or the ＋ on Focus's title bar.</b> A box arrives over your
      day. Paste a call transcript or type a line, press Return, and Jarvis
      answers in its own voice with what it added.</li>
  <li><b>It takes standing instructions, not just events.</b> "This channel
      matters most right now" or "her requests come before anyone else's"
      becomes a rule that shapes every day Jarvis builds for you afterwards.</li>
  <li><b>Your context</b>, behind the history button, holds everything you have
      told it — each note, what it became, and every rule still in force. It is
      also the only place a rule can be removed.</li>
  <li><b>One Undo.</b> Takes back the tasks, the rules and the note itself. If
      anything fails to save, Jarvis says so plainly and hands your words back
      rather than claiming it saved them.</li>
  <li>Notes never leave your Mac. They are stored and searched exactly like
      your synced mail and meetings, and become searchable by your coding
      agents through the same local connection.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
